+## Physical Constants Reference
+
+ALWAYS import from `scipy.constants` — never hardcode values:
+```python
+from scipy import constants as const
+const.c          # speed of light (m/s)
+const.h          # Planck constant (J·s)
+const.hbar       # reduced Planck constant
+const.k          # Boltzmann constant (J/K)
+const.G          # gravitational constant
+const.e          # elementary charge (C)
+const.m_e        # electron mass (kg)
+const.m_p        # proton mass (kg)
+const.epsilon_0  # vacuum permittivity
+const.mu_0       # vacuum permeability
+const.N_A        # Avogadro number
+const.R          # gas constant (J/(mol·K))
+const.sigma      # Stefan-Boltzmann constant
+const.g          # standard gravity (m/s²)
+```
+
+For unit conversions:
+```python
+const.eV         # 1 eV in Joules
+const.angstrom   # 1 Å in meters
+const.atm        # 1 atm in Pascals
+const.zero_Celsius  # 0°C in Kelvin
+```
